{"step_index":85,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:52:43Z","input_tokens":1447,"cache_read_tokens":115029,"output_tokens":6220,"content":"While that runs, I'll write the program-tree operations used by the block editor:","thinking":"I'm also planning the child login flow for /masuk with tabs for family code or class code: a server action to look up the code and return minimal child info (nickname, avatar), then a PIN keypad step to authenticate the selected child.\n\nFor \"new student\" joining a class, I need a flow collecting nickname, avatar, grade, and a self-chosen PIN, saved via a joinClass action with consent marked as teacher-confirmed. I should add brute-force protection on PINs (lock after 5 failed attempts for 5 minutes), plus an onboarding \"kenalan\" flow for avatar selection and introducing the mascot before reaching the main map.\n\nI'm structuring the child area as a protected route group with a shared layout showing avatar, nickname, stars, rank, and toggles, while /masuk stays outside that group since it doesn't need a session. I also want the layout to check today's total play duration and show a \"time for a break\" screen if the daily limit is exceeded.\n\nFor the progress endpoint, I'm deciding to have the server re-run the mission program itself to verify success rather than trusting the client, which prevents cheating. For hints and attempts, I'm weighing whether to compute everything server-side from chat logs versus trusting client-reported values, leaning toward server-side counting of hint messages since the last successful attempt on that mission for better accuracy.\n\nI'm sketching out the response shape with stars, score, feedback, badges, and next mission info, plus the Bibi chat API route with streaming responses and hint-level headers, and noting the module files needed for prompts, safety checks, and Gemini integration. I'm also outlining the mission play page flow: server-side loading of mission and progress state, redirecting if locked, then handing off to the client-side MissionPlayer component.\n\nNow I'm planning the client component breakdown — header, board view, block editor with drag-and-drop, controls, a Bibi side panel that adapts between desktop drawer and mobile bottom sheet, a result modal with stars and b\n<truncated 380 bytes>\nls so keyboard users can still manage the program.\n\nI'm also designing droppable gap zones between blocks and a trash area, with a drag overlay preview, logic to prevent dropping a block into its own subtree, and empty-container placeholders that expand visibly during dragging.\n\nFor collision detection, I'm combining pointerWithin with a closestCenter fallback so touch drags can still land precisely on the small gap zones, enlarging gaps while dragging to make hits easier.\n\nI'm also planning the pure program-state operations—insertAt, removeById, updateBlock, moveBlock—that manipulate the block tree immutably, plus a trash droppable area so dragging blocks outside the program area deletes them.\n\nI need to handle index shifting carefully when moving within the same container, track container keys like 'root' and nested body/then/else slots, and cap nesting depth at 3. For persistence, I'll store the in-progress draft program in localStorage per mission/child while actual completion progress lives in the database. For the visual runner, I'm planning CSS-transform-based movement with timed animation frames, and positioning the character using percentage-based left/top coordinates on a responsive grid board.\n\nI'm also designing the sorting animation to step items into boxes frame by frame with simple emoji feedback, syncing the highlighted block in the editor to the currently running frame, and building out a sound module with toggleable effects and a motion-reduction preference, both persisted via localStorage. Finally I'm sketching the Bibi chat panel to stream responses via a fetch reader with quick-question chips and a rating feature.\n\nFor rating, I'm having the server pre-create the Bibi chat log row with empty content so I can pass its id back in a response header, then update that row once streaming finishes, and I'll wire up a simple rate endpoint. I'm also considering adding a cheap text-to-speech button using speechSynthesis for Bibi's replies before moving on to writing the actual program operations.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"// Immutable operations on the nested block program (used by the drag-and-drop editor).\\n// A \\\"container key\\\" identifies a list of blocks: \\\"root\\\" | `${blockId}:body` | `${blockId}:then` | `${blockId}:else`.\\n\\nimport type { Block, PaletteItem } from \\\"./types\\\";\\n\\nexport type ContainerKey = string;\\nexport const ROOT: ContainerKey = \\\"root\\\";\\nexport const MAX_DEPTH = 3;\\n\\nlet counter = 0;\\nexport function newId(): string {\\n  counter += 1;\\n  return `b${Date.now().toString(36)}${counter.toString(36)}${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 6)}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function fromPalette(item: PaletteItem, defaultCond?: string): Block {\\n  switch (item.type) {\\n    case \\\"move\\\":\\n      return { id: newId(), type: \\\"move\\\", dir: item.dir };\\n    case \\\"repeat\\\":\\n      return { id: newId(), type: \\\"repeat\\\", times: item.times ?? 2, body: [] };\\n    case \\\"if\\\":\\n      return { id: newId(), type: \\\"if\\\", cond: item.cond ?? defaultCond ?? \\\"\\\", then: [], else: [] };\\n    case \\\"put\\\":\\n      return { id: newId(), type: \\\"put\\\", box: item.box };\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction childLists(b: Block): [string, Block[]][] {\\n  if (b.type === \\\"repeat\\\") return [[\\\"body\\\", b.body]];\\n  if (b.type === \\\"if\\\")\\n    return [\\n      [\\\"then\\\", b.then],\\n      [\\\"else\\\", b.else],\\n    ];\\n  return [];\\n}\\n\\nfunction withList(b: Block, slot: string, list: Block[]): Block {\\n  if (b.type === \\\"repeat\\\" && slot === \\\"body\\\") return { ...b, body: list };\\n  if (b.type === \\\"if\\\" && slot === \\\"then\\\") return { ...b, then: list };\\n  if (b.type === \\\"if\\\" && slot === \\\"else\\\") return { ...b, else: list };\\n  return b;\\n}\\n\\n/** Apply fn to the list identified by key. */\\nfunction mapList(program: Block[], key: ContainerKey, fn: (list: Block[]) => Block[]): Block[] {\\n  if (key === ROOT) return fn(program);\\n  const [ownerId, slot] = key.split(\\\":\\\");\\n  const walk = (list: Block[]): Block[] =>\\n    list.map((b) => {\\n      if (b.id === ownerId) {\\n        const current = childLists(b).find(([s]) => s === slot)?.[1];\\n        return current ? withL\n<truncated 5267 bytes>","Description":"\"Pure immutable tree ops for the nested block program + server-side sanitizer.\"","Overwrite":"false","TargetFile":"\"e:\\\\codekids\\\\src\\\\lib\\\\missions\\\\program.ts\"","toolAction":"\"Writing program operations\"","toolSummary":"\"Program operations\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking","tool_calls"]}
